<DocsLayout title="Hosting" description="Share your singleplayer world or a Paper server.">
  <h2>Host a singleplayer world</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open your world, then press <kbd>G</kbd> and choose <strong>Host this world</strong>.</li>
    <li>etmc fills in a random network name and secret, so leave them as they are.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Start hosting</strong>.</li>
    <li>Open <strong>Session status</strong> and click <strong>Copy invite link</strong>, or run
      <code>/etmc invite</code>.</li>
    <li>Send the link to your friends.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="warn"><strong>Your secret isn't protected.</strong> It's saved as plain text in <code>config/etmc.json</code>, and anyone with your link can read it and join. Keep it random, and never use a password you
    use anywhere else.</div>
  <p>Keep the world open while friends are playing. Leaving the world stops hosting.</p>

  <h2>Host a Paper server</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Download the etmc Paper jar from <a href="https://github.com/L5Z12/etmc/releases">Releases</a> and put it in
      your <code>plugins</code> folder.</li>
    <li>Create a config with the <a href="/generator">generator</a>, which suggests a random secret, and save it as
      <code>plugins/etmc/config.yml</code>.</li>
    <li>Restart the server, or run <code>/etmc reload</code>.</li>
    <li>Copy the <code>etmc://</code> link from the server log, or run <code>/etmc link</code>.</li>
    <li>Share the link with your players.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="warn"><strong>Your secret isn't protected.</strong> It's plain text in <code>config.yml</code>, and anyone with your link can read it and join. If you leave the default <code>change-me</code>, etmc replaces it with a random one. Keep it random, and never use a password you
    use anywhere else.</div>
  <p>Running a public server that anyone can join? Leave the secret empty.</p>
</DocsLayout>
